---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/prose/Prose.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/molecules/CtaBlock.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Use MRX in Your AI Assistant | Public MCP Setup"
  description="Connect a compatible AI assistant to MRX public mineral-rights guides. Find the MCP endpoint, setup steps, example questions, source links, and privacy limits."
  path="/ai-assistant/"
  pageCategory="education"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Learning Center', path: '/learning-center/' },
    { name: 'Use MRX in Your AI Assistant', path: '/ai-assistant/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Prose>
        <h1>Use MRX in your AI assistant</h1>
        <p data-answer-first="true">
          Connect a compatible AI assistant to Mineral Rights Xchange's public guides with the MRX
          Model Context Protocol (MCP) service. Ask an educational question, find relevant pages,
          and follow the source links to read the original MRX guidance.
        </p>
        <p>
          Public MCP release: <a
            href="https://github.com/underwriter-MRX/mrx-mcp/releases/tag/v0.2.0">v0.2.0</a
          >. Setup information updated September 23, 2026.
        </p>
        <h2>Connect a compatible assistant</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Use an AI client that supports remote MCP servers over HTTPS with Streamable HTTP.
          </li>
          <li>Add the server URL: <code>https://mrx-public-mcp.vercel.app/mcp</code>.</li>
          <li>
            Select no authentication if the client asks. The public MRX service requires no API key
            or MRX account.
          </li>
          <li>
            Enable the connection and ask the assistant to search MRX's public guides and include
            source links.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Connection controls and availability depend on your client, plan, and workspace settings.
          This setup page does not mean MRX is approved or listed in the ChatGPT app directory.
          Developers can use the <a href="https://github.com/underwriter-MRX/mrx-mcp#readme"
            >MRX MCP README</a
          >
          for client configuration, local installation, and troubleshooting.
        </p>
        <p>
          A fresh server instance may need time to prepare its public-content index. If your first
          request reports that the index is incomplete, wait briefly and retry. You can always use
          the <a href="/learning-center/">Learning Center</a> in your browser.
        </p>
        <h2>Try a question with source links</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            “Search MRX for inherited mineral rights. What records should I organize before a human
            review? Include the source links.”
          </li>
          <li>
            “Find MRX guides explaining why a royalty check might shrink. Separate possible causes
            from facts I would need to verify.”
          </li>
          <li>
            “Find MRX's explanation of an offer, a letter of intent, and a purchase agreement. Link
            to the original guide.”
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Read those topics directly: <a href="/inherited-mineral-rights/"
            >inherited mineral rights</a
          >,
          <a href="/blog/why-did-my-royalty-check-go-down/">why a royalty check may go down</a>, and
          <a href="/blog/mineral-rights-offer-vs-letter-of-intent-vs-purchase-agreement/"
            >offer, letter of intent, and purchase agreement differences</a
          >.
        </p>
        <h2>What the public service can do</h2>
        <p>
          Six read-only tools help a client search published guides, retrieve a public page, check
          service readiness, and find an appropriate starting point. Standard <code>search</code>
          and <code>fetch</code> tools return source-linked results. MRX-specific tools are
          <code>mrx_search_guides</code>, <code>mrx_read_page</code>, <code>mrx_status</code>, and
          <code>mrx_get_started</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Results are educational public content. They do not establish ownership, verify a
          document, determine the value of an interest, or provide individualized legal, tax, or
          investment advice. Read the cited page and consult an appropriately qualified professional
          for decisions that require one.
        </p>
        <h2>Keep personal information private</h2>
        <p>
          The MCP service cannot access private customer accounts or documents, change records, book
          appointments, or submit a request for you. Do not include personal documents, account
          numbers, contact details, or other private information in MCP questions.
        </p>
        <p>
          The application processes requests transiently and caches public source content in memory.
          Vercel retains operational and security logs, and your AI provider has its own data
          policies. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/#public-mrx-mcp-service"
            >public MCP privacy disclosure</a
          >
          before connecting.
        </p>
        <h2>Continue with a human review</h2>
        <p>
          Use the guides to organize your questions, then <a href="/book/"
            >request a free MRX review</a
          >
          when you want to discuss your situation with the team. Connecting an assistant or receiving
          an AI answer does not start or complete a human review.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBlock
    title="Choose your next step"
    body="Browse the public guides or request a conversation with the MRX team about your situation."
    primaryCta={{
      label: 'Explore the Learning Center',
      href: '/learning-center/',
      ctaName: 'mcp-learning-center',
    }}
    secondaryCta={{ label: 'Request a Free Review', href: '/book/', ctaName: 'mcp-human-review' }}
  />
</MarketingLayout>
